# oracle: two peri/pmb blocks that were never bonded collide (64 + 64 atoms, an oblique impact at 300 m/s each, 100 steps): the short-range contact force acts between every pair of the neighbor list, and the pressure carries the atom volumes
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 2.9e-12, atoms 1.4e-12. Before the fix the blocks passed through each other (pe 0 throughout; native collides at step 40).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all rel=1e-8 atoms=all
units           si
boundary        s s s
atom_style      peri
atom_modify     map array
neighbor        0.0010 bin
lattice         sc 0.0005
region          box block 0 12 0 4 0 4 units lattice
create_box      1 box
region          a block 0 3.5 0 3.5 0 3.5 units lattice
region          b block 7.5 11.5 0 3.5 0 3.5 units lattice
create_atoms    1 region a
create_atoms    1 region b
group           a region a
group           b region b
pair_style      peri/pmb
pair_coeff      * * 1.6863e22 0.0015001 0.0005 0.25
set             group all density 2200
set             group all volume 1.25e-10
velocity        a set 300 0 0 units box
velocity        b set -300 60 -40 units box
fix             1 all nve
compute         1 all damage/atom
compute         2 all reduce sum c_1
timestep        1.0e-7
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal c_2 press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          10
run             100
